<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The driver (cross-links round three, G1 with G2; Framework 0.113.0; docs/development/vehicle-crosslinks.md). The owner's
    answer (13 Nov 2026): a driver's health, drugs and tiredness slow every vehicle, gently, at worst x0.7 of speed, and nothing is ever
    crashed for it. The game's own capacities carry every cause (DriverRule): pain, drugs, a concussion, hypothermia and heatstroke lower
    consciousness, so a freezing cab slows the vehicle through the game's own conditions with no second model; a lost eye lowers sight; a
    broken hand lowers manipulation. A tired driver (the game's "tired" rest level) is a tenth less fit. The fittest person in a driving seat
    counts; a trailer, an autonomous vehicle or an empty one reads fit. Its own system, so a player can switch it off in the settings' list
    of systems. A worse driver also wears tyres and brakes up to x1.1 (the running gear's and brakes' wear flows read driverFitness).
    Every stage edge and factor is authored. Not yet tested in game.
    Framework 0.190.0 (EM11, hours on type): driverExperience, the practice of whoever in a driving seat knows this kind of vehicle best.
    It eases brake and tyre wear down to x0.85 (their wear flows read it) and, in C#, a landing's wear on an aircraft down to x0.6. Never
    speed. Half of it after 40 hours at the wheel of this kind (PracticeRule, authored).
  -->
  <Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
    <defName>PhobosVehicleSystem_Driver</defName>
    <label>driver</label>
    <description>Whoever is at the wheel. A driver who is hurt, drugged, half-blind, one-handed or tired drives slower and harder on the vehicle. Nothing is ever crashed for it: rest, medicine or a fresh driver put it right.</description>
    <quantities>
      <li>
        <name>driverFitness</name>
        <description>How fit the driver is to drive: awake and clear-headed, able to see, with the use of their hands, and rested.</description>
        <label>driver</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Driver" />
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.6</to>
            <label>badly impaired</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_StatFactor">
                <stat>MoveSpeed</stat>
                <factor>0.7</factor>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgDriverImpaired</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.6</from>
            <to>0.8</to>
            <label>impaired</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_StatFactor">
                <stat>MoveSpeed</stat>
                <factor>0.8</factor>
              </li>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgDriverImpaired</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.8</from>
            <to>0.95</to>
            <label>driving carefully</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_StatFactor">
                <stat>MoveSpeed</stat>
                <factor>0.9</factor>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <name>driverExperience</name>
        <description>How well the driver knows this kind of vehicle, from the hours they have spent at the wheel of one. A practised driver is easier on the brakes and tyres, and a practised pilot lands more gently. It never makes anyone faster.</description>
        <label>driver's practice</label>
        <unit>Fraction</unit>
        <min>0</min>
        <max>1</max>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Driver">
            <reading>Experience</reading>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <to>0.25</to>
            <label>new to it</label>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.25</from>
            <to>0.75</to>
            <label>getting used to it</label>
          </li>
          <li>
            <from>0.75</from>
            <label>seasoned</label>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- G2: one message when the driver tires; the slowing itself is in driverFitness above. -->
        <name>driverTired</name>
        <description>Whether the driver is tired.</description>
        <label>driver tired</label>
        <unit>OnOff</unit>
        <hidden>true</hidden>
        <derivedFrom>
          <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Input_Driver">
            <reading>Tired</reading>
          </li>
        </derivedFrom>
        <stages>
          <li>
            <from>0.5</from>
            <label>tired</label>
            <notable>true</notable>
            <effects>
              <li Class="Phobos.VehicleSystems.Effect_Message">
                <message>PhobosVehicleSystems_MsgDriverTired</message>
                <type>CautionInput</type>
              </li>
            </effects>
          </li>
        </stages>
      </li>
    </quantities>
  </Phobos.VehicleSystems.PhobosVehicleSystemDef>
</Defs>
